        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T07:27:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, does this prevent us from doing the __builtin_available check that we will be doing? If so, no. If not, yes.\n\nWhy do you want to fallback to sdk_version in case when min_sdk_version is not set? Can\u0027t we just set min_sdk_version anyway?",
      "parentUuid": "b22754b2_f335faf0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2861,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2863,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "f9b9204a5af70b1e6fe224097da7a60bc2dae726",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a84104fd_196318c0",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2863,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T09:07:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general apex variants don\u0027t have sdk_version because sdk mutator clears sdk_version for platform variants and apex variants are based on platform variants. By the way, when a native module sets \"sdk_variant_only\", apex will bundle \"sdk\" variant of the module (and its transitive deps from \"sdk\" variants as well). For those sdk variants which set \"sdk_version\", setting \"min_sdk_version\" seems to be redundant. This fallback happens only when it is apex variant and also sdk variant.\n\nYeah, instead we could set min_sdk_version. eg for libbase_ndk, libfmt_ndk, .. \n\nIn fact, I ran into this with sdkext apex with derive_sdk. aosp/1287137 tried to make derive_sdk cc_binary a normal apex variant but it gets reverted with some selinux violations. However, at the moment, I thought people(at least, Anton) might get confused when they find that sdk variant(or its sdk_version setting) is not used for apex.\n\nHonestly, I\u0027m not sure which is better: enforcing strictly on min_sdk_version, or fallback to sdk_version (for sdk variants). For me both seems fine. ;)\n\nIf you still have concerns about fallback behavior, I\u0027m fine to revert it.",
      "parentUuid": "df3b24f0_4149d5e6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2861,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2863,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "f9b9204a5af70b1e6fe224097da7a60bc2dae726",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "159e8c68_84f652de",
