      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T09:58:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For now, there is no checks about relation between sdk_version and min_sdk_version.\n\nUseSdk() is required because sdkMutator clears Sdk_version property for non-sdk variants. \n\n  cc_library{\n   name: \"foo\",\n   sdk_version: \"current\",\n   min_sdk_version: \"29\",\n   apex_available: [\"com.foo\"],\n   ..\n  }\n\nFor the library \"foo\", sdk variant has sdk_version: current, but platform variant and apex(com.foo) variant doesn\u0027t have sdk_version. So we can\u0027t fallback to it in most cases. Very confusing. ;-)\n\nI\u0027ll remove the fallback behavior. I think it is just adding complexity on top of already complicated things.",
      "parentUuid": "159e8c68_84f652de",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2861,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2863,
        "endChar": 2
      },
